  "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B004",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of distinct T- and B-lymphocyte lineages and their roles in adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B018",
    "B032"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B004 remains the most sharply defined discovery: the distinction of T- and B-lymphocyte lineages established the cellular organization of adaptive immunity. Its explanatory and medical importance has been tested and extended over decades, while Miller and Cooper represent complementary, compact credit for the specified lineage-defining discoveries. On comparison with B018, B004 has similarly exceptional maturity and bounded attribution but supplies the broader organizing principle for immune physiology.",
    "case_against": "The history of lymphocyte biology included other important investigators. A final citation must therefore credit Miller and Cooper for the particular lineage-defining discoveries without implying that they alone account for the full development of adaptive immunology. B018 has a comparably mature and focused two-person mechanism, while B032 has unusually large direct therapeutic consequences; each remains a serious alternative.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson prefers B032 because GLP-1 physiology has enabled transformative treatment of diabetes and obesity, while recognizing uncertainty over assigning the maximum three-person credit across physiology, optimization, and translation.",
        "response": "I continue to give substantial weight to the therapeutic transformation, but the credit and prize-definition issue remains central after reassessment. A citation limited to physiology still requires a historically complete account of who made the enabling discoveries, distinct from later drug development. B004 more cleanly identifies one biological principle and a complementary two-person contribution."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
        "point": "El-Manira supports B004 but cautions that the two-person citation must be confined to the lineage-defining work rather than the wider community development of lymphocyte biology.",
        "response": "I agree with that limitation and would make it explicit in the final framing. The proposed citation is defensible only as recognition of the distinct T- and B-lineage discoveries and their roles in adaptive immunity; it should not be read as credit for every subsequent advance in lymphocyte biology."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "svenningsson-per",
        "point": "Svenningsson regards B018 as an exceptionally clear and fundamental alternative, credited to Hartl and Horwich for chaperonin-assisted folding.",
        "response": "That comparison has reinforced rather than displaced my preference. B018 is perhaps the closest alternative in mechanistic clarity and mature attribution. I retain B004 because the lineage distinction provided the cellular logic for adaptive immunity as a whole, with equivalent durability and a similarly concise awardable account."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical documentation can delimit Miller's and Cooper's respective lineage-defining contributions precisely enough for the proposed two-person citation.",
      "Whether comparative assessment should instead favor B018's focused cellular mechanism or B032's exceptional therapeutic consequences despite their different attribution questions."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific connection is apparent from the supplied profile. It documents co-authorship with committee member Per Svenningsson; the chair summary also notes a 2009 co-authored paper with Abdel El-Manira. Neither identifies a connection to the proposed candidates or achievement."
  }
}
